<title>UK: Royal Bank says credit card spending higher.</title>
<headline>Royal Bank says credit card spending higher.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Royal Bank of Scotland Plc said on Monday its credit card customers spent nearly 125 million stg in the first 20 days of December, a rise of 30 percent on the year-earlier period.</p>
<p>The bank said cash withdrawals from its 1,170 automated cash dispensers nationwide were up nine percent in the first 19 days of the month at 263 million stg.</p>
<p>The bank said the average credit card transaction rose 6.6 percent to almost 52 stg.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
